## MAIN DOCUMENT STRUCTURE (EXACT ORDER)

Header (`# BizTalk Technical Design — {app_name}` + Source / Generated / Agent line), then:

| # | Section | Marker | Phase | Reference icon |
|---|---------|--------|-------|----------------|
| 1 | Application Overview | `<!-- SECTION:1 -->` | 0 | 📦 |
| 2 | Architecture | `<!-- SECTION:2 -->` | 0 | — (📦 inherited) |
| 3 | Orchestration Documentation | `<!-- SECTION:3 -->` | 1 | 🔀 |
| 4 | Schemas & Data Mappings | `<!-- SECTION:4 -->` | 2 | 🗂️ 🔗 |
| 5 | Pipelines, Ports & Helpers | `<!-- SECTION:5 -->` | 3 | 🧩 |
| 6 | MuleSoft Replication Readiness | `<!-- SECTION:6 -->` | 4 | 🚧 |
| 7 | Validation & Certification | `<!-- SECTION:7 -->` | 5 | 📋 |

> Heavy detail (verbatim expressions, full field trees, all map links, full helper code) lives in supporting docs; the main doc carries the narrative + diagrams + the complete Section 4/6 tables. Full literal per-section templates: `templates/documentation-template-guide.md`.

